<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK construction firms manage complex projects across multiple sites, with subcontractors, suppliers, and compliance requirements all demanding attention. Bespoke software can help you track projects in real-time, manage compliance, and give directors the visibility they need to make informed decisions - but most firms are still relying on spreadsheets, paper site reports, and accounting software that wasn't built for construction project management.</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf construction software rarely matches how UK contractors actually work. Generic project management tools don't understand construction programmes, dependencies, or the relationship between design, procurement, and build phases. Accounting software handles invoicing but can't track costs against specific work packages or manage retention payments across long contracts. Site reporting apps built for general use can't capture the specific data your contracts require - whether that's RIDDOR reportable incidents, daily plant utilisation, or subcontractor CIS verification. The result is project managers spending evenings reconciling spreadsheets instead of managing projects.</p>
<p>We build custom software for UK construction firms - from project management platforms and site reporting apps to subcontractor management and health and safety systems. We understand construction workflows, from the site office to the boardroom, and we build systems that integrate with your existing accounting and job costing tools. Whether it's a bespoke site reporting app that captures photos, progress, and issues against specific plot numbers, or a subcontractor management system that handles CIS verification and payment applications automatically, bespoke software fits your exact processes.</p>
<p>Construction compliance carries serious consequences. CDM 2015 regulations, RIDDOR reporting, CIS compliance, and health and safety audits all demand meticulous record-keeping. Bespoke software can automate CDM duty-holder tracking, maintain digital health and safety files per project, flag subcontractor CIS status changes, and generate HSE-ready incident reports - replacing paper-based systems that are easily lost on site and impossible to search during an audit.</p>
<p>A UK main contractor managing £30 million of projects across five live sites was struggling to produce accurate month-end cost reports. Their accounting software couldn't track committed costs against work packages, and project managers maintained separate spreadsheets that never reconciled. We built a bespoke project cost tracking system that integrated with their existing Sage setup and captured committed costs in real time. Month-end cost reports that previously took five days to produce were available on the first of every month, and the firm identified £180,000 of unbilled variations within three months of going live.</p>
<p>Construction is a sector where bespoke software delivers clear ROI. Projects generate vast amounts of data - budgets, programmes, site reports, compliance records. The opportunity is building software that turns that data into real-time project visibility, automated compliance, and better decision-making.</p>

